1
00:00:05,276 --> 00:00:07,412
<i>I must do what I need to.</i>

2
00:00:08,413 --> 00:00:10,949
<i>I cannot forgive anyone who threatens</i>

3
00:00:12,917 --> 00:00:14,352
<i>Mariko's happiness.</i>

4
00:00:14,853 --> 00:00:17,856
<i>If this person deleted the data…</i>

5
00:00:17,922 --> 00:00:19,524
How creepy!

6
00:00:19,591 --> 00:00:22,093
-Are you her stalker or something?
-And I also won't forgive you

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,662
if you try to scheme
against Mariko any further.

8
00:00:24,729 --> 00:00:26,297
Mariko!

9
00:00:27,398 --> 00:00:29,033
What? What's up?

10
00:00:30,001 --> 00:00:33,338
The person I wanted to ride
the Ferris wheel with is you.

11
00:00:34,472 --> 00:00:35,640
I…

12
00:00:36,908 --> 00:00:38,042
<i>I've always…</i>

13
00:00:38,877 --> 00:00:40,411
<i>It's fine.</i>

14
00:00:41,012 --> 00:00:42,480
<i>I know how…</i>

15
00:00:44,516 --> 00:00:45,850
<i>to protect Mariko.</i>

16
00:00:57,362 --> 00:00:59,063
-Sorry.
-No, it's fine.

17
00:01:07,505 --> 00:01:10,141
Oh, wait, uh…

18
00:01:10,909 --> 00:01:11,809
Mariko.

19
00:01:13,111 --> 00:01:14,045
Wait.

20
00:01:17,949 --> 00:01:19,217
What?

21
00:01:21,252 --> 00:01:23,821
What do you mean "what"?

22
00:01:28,626 --> 00:01:29,694
‎Ah, uh…

23
00:01:41,105 --> 00:01:42,874
TAISUKE SAKURA

24
00:01:42,941 --> 00:01:45,677
IT LOOKS LIKE YUKIMURA WENT
TO THE SAME MIDDLE AND HIGH SCHOOL AS YOU

25
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:54,953
Did you go to Rinka Academy
for middle and high school?

26
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,661
Yes.

27
00:02:08,533 --> 00:02:10,201
Does that mean…

28
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:13,905
we were classmates?

29
00:02:13,972 --> 00:02:15,139
Did you know?

30
00:02:17,075 --> 00:02:17,909
Yes.

31
00:02:28,553 --> 00:02:29,621
I see…

32
00:02:56,447 --> 00:02:59,651
IT LOOKS LIKE YUKIMURA WENT
TO THE SAME MIDDLE AND HIGH SCHOOL AS YOU

33
00:03:19,504 --> 00:03:20,972
MARIKO NOSE

34
00:03:30,682 --> 00:03:32,317
SOTA YUKIMURA

35
00:03:32,383 --> 00:03:33,618
There he is…

36
00:03:51,436 --> 00:03:53,404
SOTA YUKIMURA

37
00:04:16,527 --> 00:04:17,729
<i>It's over.</i>

38
00:04:18,563 --> 00:04:20,531
My 25-year crush.

39
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:24,168
Doesn't this mean
she has actually accepted it?

40
00:04:26,204 --> 00:04:30,174
Knowing Mariko, if she wanted to say no,
wouldn't she have said so?

41
00:04:32,076 --> 00:04:33,211
She would.

42
00:04:33,277 --> 00:04:36,447
Which means, at the very least,
you weren't rejected.

43
00:04:50,595 --> 00:04:51,763
So it's not over?

44
00:04:51,829 --> 00:04:53,765
If anything, it might finally be starting.

45
00:04:53,831 --> 00:04:54,732
What?

46
00:04:55,767 --> 00:04:56,734
Isn't that great?

47
00:04:57,335 --> 00:05:00,071
It means even after showing her
your true self, it was totally fine.

48
00:05:06,577 --> 00:05:08,546
My true self…

49
00:05:12,216 --> 00:05:15,586
What? You went to the same
middle and high school too?

50
00:05:16,454 --> 00:05:17,321
Yes.

51
00:05:18,823 --> 00:05:20,725
What are the odds?

52
00:05:22,794 --> 00:05:25,163
This finally makes sense.

53
00:05:26,431 --> 00:05:29,700
I always had this feeling with Yukimura,

54
00:05:29,767 --> 00:05:32,203
like things didn't really need
much explanation.

55
00:05:33,471 --> 00:05:35,540
Like we shared a common language.

56
00:05:35,606 --> 00:05:36,541
A common language?

57
00:05:36,607 --> 00:05:37,542
Yes.

58
00:05:38,075 --> 00:05:39,610
So that means

59
00:05:39,677 --> 00:05:45,116
the person Yukimura has been in love with
this whole time was you, right, Mariko?

60
00:05:48,753 --> 00:05:50,555
Oh, what? That's…

61
00:05:50,621 --> 00:05:53,124
No matter how you look at it, it's true.

62
00:05:54,358 --> 00:05:57,995
Doesn't that mean he's been
admiring you all this time?

63
00:06:10,007 --> 00:06:10,942
Could he be a stalker?

64
00:06:11,709 --> 00:06:14,479
Given the circumstances,
the primary suspect

65
00:06:14,545 --> 00:06:16,981
remains Sota Yukimura,
who was caught on security camera

66
00:06:17,048 --> 00:06:18,182
near the scene of Tateiwa's murder.

67
00:06:18,249 --> 00:06:19,083
On the other hand,

68
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:21,385
Mariko Nose, who was in a power struggle
with him at the company,

69
00:06:21,452 --> 00:06:23,821
has the strongest motive to hate Tateiwa.

70
00:06:23,888 --> 00:06:26,958
Multiple employees
also witnessed them arguing

71
00:06:27,024 --> 00:06:29,227
at the office on the day of the incident.

72
00:06:29,293 --> 00:06:32,997
However, Mariko Nose has a solid alibi.

73
00:06:33,064 --> 00:06:36,267
In that case, right now, just for her,

74
00:06:36,334 --> 00:06:39,370
this guy, Sota, did this to Tateiwa?

75
00:06:40,071 --> 00:06:44,475
Committing crimes on his own motive
for the woman he loves?

76
00:06:44,542 --> 00:06:47,945
That really is the mindset of a stalker.

77
00:06:48,012 --> 00:06:49,680
SOTA YUKIMURA

78
00:07:16,407 --> 00:07:17,575
Um…

79
00:07:20,811 --> 00:07:22,246
Could we talk a little about

80
00:07:23,114 --> 00:07:25,349
what happened the other day?

81
00:07:29,787 --> 00:07:32,990
You really were in the yearbook.

82
00:07:34,258 --> 00:07:35,126
Yes.

83
00:07:36,327 --> 00:07:38,362
-I was.
-Why didn't you tell me?

84
00:07:41,799 --> 00:07:43,167
Um…

85
00:07:43,968 --> 00:07:47,371
You probably didn't remember who I was.

86
00:07:48,306 --> 00:07:52,610
It'd be awkward if someone you didn't
remember said you were together.

87
00:07:57,148 --> 00:07:58,215
That's true.

88
00:08:00,318 --> 00:08:02,019
I might have just said,
"So what?" or something.

89
00:08:10,027 --> 00:08:12,229
That MP3 player
back then was yours, wasn't it?

90
00:08:13,731 --> 00:08:15,466
Didn't you have one when we were students?

91
00:08:15,533 --> 00:08:18,369
Did it have a Kogepan sticker on the back?

92
00:08:20,004 --> 00:08:20,838
Yes.

93
00:08:22,707 --> 00:08:23,741
What do you mean?

94
00:08:32,516 --> 00:08:34,619
‎FESTIVAL

95
00:08:37,722 --> 00:08:38,923
-It's a secret.
-What?

96
00:08:40,725 --> 00:08:42,760
-What do you mean?
-Because you're not fair.

97
00:08:50,701 --> 00:08:55,473
I didn't quite understand
you before, Yukimura.

98
00:08:57,541 --> 00:08:59,176
But things finally make sense now.

99
00:09:04,882 --> 00:09:07,885
I'm glad I got to know the real you.

100
00:09:19,096 --> 00:09:21,332
Did you commute by train, Yukimura?

101
00:09:21,399 --> 00:09:22,466
Yes.

102
00:09:22,533 --> 00:09:25,703
I waited at that railroad crossing
that never opened every single day.

103
00:09:26,671 --> 00:09:28,639
Did you know? The station was renovated,

104
00:09:28,706 --> 00:09:30,307
so you don't have to cross
that railway anymore.

105
00:09:30,374 --> 00:09:31,375
What?

106
00:09:31,442 --> 00:09:33,911
They even built a ticket gate
on the opposite side.

107
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:40,985
That must be convenient, but in its own
way, that crossing was part of our youth.

108
00:09:41,052 --> 00:09:42,853
You think so?

109
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:46,023
I wish they had upgraded it sooner.

110
00:09:46,924 --> 00:09:50,127
Do you know how many times I almost
ran late and had to sprint because of it?

111
00:09:50,194 --> 00:09:52,963
Mariko, the reason you almost ran late
wasn't because of the railroad crossing.

112
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:54,999
It was because you overslept.

113
00:09:55,866 --> 00:09:58,903
Even though you're usually so reliable,
you're terrible in the mornings.

114
00:09:58,969 --> 00:10:01,038
Did that fix itself
once you entered the workforce?

115
00:10:02,273 --> 00:10:06,377
How do you know that? That I used
to oversleep and almost run late?

116
00:10:07,244 --> 00:10:09,780
Well, I wouldn't say I knew for sure…

117
00:10:12,083 --> 00:10:13,350
I just figured

118
00:10:14,018 --> 00:10:17,288
most people sprinting
because they're late probably overslept.

119
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:22,460
Well, sure, yes.

120
00:10:23,327 --> 00:10:24,161
That's true.

121
00:10:26,063 --> 00:10:26,931
You know,

122
00:10:27,765 --> 00:10:29,500
sometimes you give off this vibe,

123
00:10:29,567 --> 00:10:33,070
like you saw everything back then.

124
00:10:40,711 --> 00:10:42,680
I suddenly really want to eat that again!

125
00:10:42,747 --> 00:10:48,252
The school cafeteria's
minced meat croquette.

126
00:10:48,319 --> 00:10:50,554
-Ah, that triangle one!
-That triangle one.

127
00:10:51,288 --> 00:10:52,957
You remember!

128
00:10:53,657 --> 00:10:55,526
I've never seen it anywhere else.

129
00:10:55,593 --> 00:10:56,927
-That's true.
-For the most part.

130
00:11:16,013 --> 00:11:17,648
<i>August 13.</i>

131
00:11:18,616 --> 00:11:19,517
<i>Today,</i>

132
00:11:20,317 --> 00:11:23,254
<i>Mariko and I talked about memories</i>
<i>from middle and high school.</i>

133
00:11:25,356 --> 00:11:28,259
<i>In all these 25 years, a day like this…</i>

134
00:11:34,932 --> 00:11:38,169
<i>In all these 25 years, a day like this…</i>

135
00:11:43,007 --> 00:11:44,275
<i>A day like…</i>

136
00:11:47,545 --> 00:11:49,013
<i>A day… A day…</i>

137
00:11:49,079 --> 00:11:51,749
<i>A day like this… A day like this…</i>

138
00:11:56,921 --> 00:12:00,090
<i>A day like this, I never would</i>
<i>have believed it'd ever come.</i>

139
00:12:02,026 --> 00:12:03,294
<i>And so I</i>

140
00:12:04,361 --> 00:12:05,863
<i>bought fried potatoes.</i>

141
00:12:12,636 --> 00:12:14,905
‎MARIKO UPLOADED A NEW POST

142
00:12:18,943 --> 00:12:22,046
COULDN'T RESIST THESE ON MY WAY HOME

143
00:12:26,083 --> 00:12:29,286
‎GRADUATION BOOK

144
00:12:33,958 --> 00:12:35,492
SOTA YUKIMURA

145
00:12:51,175 --> 00:12:52,042
<i>However…</i>

146
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:55,746
<i>I can't just get carried away.</i>

147
00:12:55,813 --> 00:12:57,615
MARIKO

148
00:13:03,187 --> 00:13:05,589
GOOD THING
YOU DIDN'T GET EXPOSED AS A STALKER

149
00:13:05,656 --> 00:13:08,993
<i>How does this person know my social media?</i>

150
00:13:11,128 --> 00:13:14,498
<i>Ever since then, I haven't been able</i>
<i>to get Sayuri out of my mind.</i>

151
00:13:18,035 --> 00:13:20,738
<i>To think my mind is consumed</i>
<i>by a woman other than Mariko…</i>

152
00:13:20,804 --> 00:13:21,839
PHOTOS

153
00:13:21,906 --> 00:13:24,375
<i>What an outrageous state of affairs.</i>

154
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:27,978
ARTICLES

155
00:13:38,355 --> 00:13:40,624
NOSE PRESIDENT'S WIFE

156
00:13:40,691 --> 00:13:44,762
DIES IN APPARENT FALL FROM BRIDGE

157
00:13:44,828 --> 00:13:46,196
FOUND LYING ON RIVERBANK

158
00:13:46,263 --> 00:13:47,998
PRONOUNCED DEAD

159
00:13:48,065 --> 00:13:49,934
CONSIDERED A SUICIDE

160
00:13:54,171 --> 00:13:57,608
Her mother died so easily
and gave up her position.

161
00:13:58,842 --> 00:14:01,278
But in that regard,
she's not like her mother at all.

162
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:05,249
<i>I want Mariko to smile.</i>

163
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:07,751
<i>That's all.</i>

164
00:14:08,719 --> 00:14:13,057
So Mariko didn't recognize Yukimura,

165
00:14:13,123 --> 00:14:15,326
but he's always had
one-sided feelings for her?

166
00:14:18,796 --> 00:14:20,998
I want things to work out for Sota.

167
00:14:21,966 --> 00:14:25,769
Having your feelings returned
by the person you love is a miracle,

168
00:14:25,836 --> 00:14:29,373
but I think finding someone you love
in the first place is the real miracle.

169
00:14:32,609 --> 00:14:33,711
I envy him.

170
00:14:36,547 --> 00:14:38,816
Izumi, when you asked me

171
00:14:38,882 --> 00:14:42,786
if I wanted to date the other day, the old
me would have said yes immediately.

172
00:14:43,921 --> 00:14:44,955
We get along great.

173
00:14:47,458 --> 00:14:48,759
And talking to you is fun.

174
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:55,899
But looking at Sota,
I realized that's not how it should be.

175
00:15:02,473 --> 00:15:04,141
Not everyone is the same.

176
00:15:07,344 --> 00:15:10,280
How much you fall for someone,

177
00:15:10,347 --> 00:15:12,816
how deep you get into it,

178
00:15:12,883 --> 00:15:15,986
isn't that different for everyone?

179
00:15:19,757 --> 00:15:21,625
I have to get going.

180
00:15:21,692 --> 00:15:24,094
The supermarket in front of the station
is giving away discounts at this time.

181
00:15:31,668 --> 00:15:33,971
Let's date.

182
00:15:39,176 --> 00:15:41,812
Okay. Let's do it.

183
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:46,450
This is the exact amount. It was great.

184
00:15:46,517 --> 00:15:48,452
I'll text you later!

185
00:15:49,153 --> 00:15:50,521
Bye-bye!

186
00:15:51,822 --> 00:15:56,093
So casual and so abrupt!

187
00:16:10,908 --> 00:16:12,910
GORO KIKUTA OFFICE

188
00:16:12,976 --> 00:16:14,812
-Yes?
-Excuse me.

189
00:16:15,579 --> 00:16:18,148
Do you have a moment to talk?

190
00:16:18,916 --> 00:16:20,551
‎TAISUKE SAKURA

191
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:27,691
No, I didn't receive
any request like that.

192
00:16:31,128 --> 00:16:32,863
That's strange.

193
00:16:32,930 --> 00:16:34,264
On July 20,

194
00:16:34,798 --> 00:16:37,201
an email was sent from you to Tateiwa,

195
00:16:37,267 --> 00:16:40,304
stating that what he requested

196
00:16:41,205 --> 00:16:42,639
was completed.

197
00:16:45,042 --> 00:16:47,411
REGARDING WHAT I ASKED YOU TO DO

198
00:16:50,614 --> 00:16:52,416
I'm sorry. Please give me a break.

199
00:16:52,483 --> 00:16:53,750
I have a duty of confidentiality.

200
00:16:53,817 --> 00:16:55,919
I can't show this to anyone
other than the client.

201
00:16:55,986 --> 00:17:00,190
This could be crucial evidence
regarding a murder case.

202
00:17:01,892 --> 00:17:03,894
Even if you refuse,

203
00:17:03,961 --> 00:17:09,166
obtaining a warrant from the court
will guarantee a disclosure order.

204
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,669
In that case,

205
00:17:13,270 --> 00:17:15,272
does that mean
it's better for me to show you now?

206
00:17:16,573 --> 00:17:17,574
Well…

207
00:17:18,442 --> 00:17:19,943
I didn't say that.

208
00:17:22,279 --> 00:17:25,682
Um, I have nothing to do with this, okay?

209
00:17:27,384 --> 00:17:30,120
We usually only get
infidelity investigations here.

210
00:17:31,088 --> 00:17:32,689
I assumed it was something like that.

211
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:43,167
I really am completely uninvolved!

212
00:17:44,034 --> 00:17:45,569
Have you shown this to anyone else?

213
00:17:46,737 --> 00:17:47,971
I swear to God.

214
00:17:48,605 --> 00:17:51,909
Showing it to anyone besides the client
would violate confidentiality.

215
00:17:53,710 --> 00:17:56,413
It's the truth, I swear! It is!

216
00:17:57,481 --> 00:18:01,418
By the way, does this person
look familiar to you?

217
00:18:06,723 --> 00:18:09,259
No, I have no idea.

218
00:18:09,927 --> 00:18:12,196
I mean, nobody could tell who that is.

219
00:18:12,796 --> 00:18:13,630
Really?

220
00:18:15,332 --> 00:18:16,366
That's right.

221
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,869
I have to make a call.

222
00:18:18,936 --> 00:18:21,071
-Oh, go ahead.
-I'm sorry.

223
00:18:21,138 --> 00:18:22,506
Excuse me.

224
00:18:44,361 --> 00:18:47,097
Hello. This is Sakura
from the first investigation division.

225
00:18:54,238 --> 00:18:55,973
Is this arrangement all right?

226
00:18:56,039 --> 00:18:57,808
Yes, thank you very much.

227
00:18:58,575 --> 00:19:01,878
This shop has been here
for quite a long time, hasn't it?

228
00:19:01,945 --> 00:19:03,714
Yes, indeed.

229
00:19:04,348 --> 00:19:06,283
It's been 25 years now.

230
00:19:07,317 --> 00:19:08,418
I see.

231
00:19:08,485 --> 00:19:09,853
Twenty-five years…

232
00:19:14,157 --> 00:19:17,027
-Hello!
-Hello.

233
00:19:17,094 --> 00:19:19,696
-How old is he?
-Three months now.

234
00:19:19,763 --> 00:19:21,198
He's gotten big.

235
00:19:21,265 --> 00:19:22,666
-I'm doing some shopping.
-Take care.

236
00:19:22,733 --> 00:19:24,668
-Yes, thank you. See you.
-Yup.

237
00:19:32,943 --> 00:19:35,379
That one has an interesting shape,
doesn't it?

238
00:19:35,912 --> 00:19:36,747
Yes.

239
00:19:37,281 --> 00:19:40,250
It doesn't need to grow straight upward.

240
00:19:40,317 --> 00:19:43,020
That shape suits it best.

241
00:19:45,889 --> 00:19:47,324
So?

242
00:19:47,391 --> 00:19:50,227
What did you want to ask me today?

243
00:19:52,162 --> 00:19:53,063
Or rather,

244
00:19:55,532 --> 00:19:57,167
what is it you really want to ask?

245
00:20:01,371 --> 00:20:04,641
Twenty-five years ago,
you were working in the Detective Division

246
00:20:04,708 --> 00:20:06,843
at the Kinuta Nishi
Police Station, weren't you?

247
00:20:07,978 --> 00:20:10,047
I'd like you to tell me about this case.

248
00:20:15,585 --> 00:20:16,720
Who are you?

249
00:20:24,628 --> 00:20:25,829
Here.

250
00:20:25,896 --> 00:20:29,166
By the time I arrived at the scene,
she was already unconscious.

251
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:31,201
She was rushed to the hospital,

252
00:20:31,268 --> 00:20:34,571
but they said she likely died instantly
upon impact from the fall.

253
00:20:34,638 --> 00:20:36,206
-Go ahead.
-Alright!

254
00:20:40,177 --> 00:20:43,780
<i>At first, we thought</i>
<i>she just slipped and fell,</i>

255
00:20:43,847 --> 00:20:48,352
but people started questioning how someone
could fall when they weren't even drunk.

256
00:20:48,418 --> 00:20:51,555
You mean it was a spot where you couldn't
fall unless you leaned over the edge?

257
00:20:51,621 --> 00:20:52,622
Yes.

258
00:20:53,123 --> 00:20:57,461
And the railing wasn't
damaged either. In that case…

259
00:20:57,527 --> 00:20:59,329
It was either suicide or murder.

260
00:21:02,099 --> 00:21:03,233
However,

261
00:21:03,767 --> 00:21:08,305
according to forensics, the fingerprints
left on the bridge railing…

262
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:11,875
looked like this.

263
00:21:14,244 --> 00:21:17,447
So, she must have gone over like this.

264
00:21:18,949 --> 00:21:21,184
Meaning she was pushed by someone, right?

265
00:21:21,251 --> 00:21:23,220
I can't say for certain,

266
00:21:23,286 --> 00:21:25,756
but that's what all of us investigators,

267
00:21:25,822 --> 00:21:28,358
including myself, thought
was the most reasonable conclusion.

268
00:21:28,959 --> 00:21:30,994
Then why…

269
00:21:31,061 --> 00:21:32,295
HEAD OFFICE SAYS SUICIDE
INVESTIGATION CLOSED

270
00:21:32,362 --> 00:21:34,531
"Head office says suicide.

271
00:21:35,432 --> 00:21:37,200
Investigation closed."

272
00:21:38,101 --> 00:21:40,837
‎THE SCENE

273
00:22:22,412 --> 00:22:25,348
GORO KIKUTA OFFICE

274
00:22:29,152 --> 00:22:30,420
Welcome home.

275
00:22:31,087 --> 00:22:32,255
Hello.

276
00:22:32,322 --> 00:22:36,693
Hey, is it true that Tado is taking over
as director in place of Tateiwa?

277
00:22:38,595 --> 00:22:40,931
Isn't he from Planning?

278
00:22:40,997 --> 00:22:42,365
Is that going to be okay?

279
00:22:42,432 --> 00:22:44,234
Besides, he's only been with us
for about five years.

280
00:22:44,301 --> 00:22:45,469
Enough.

281
00:22:46,536 --> 00:22:49,639
Stop interfering
in company personnel affairs.

282
00:22:52,576 --> 00:22:55,345
You seem to be coming
in and out of the company constantly,

283
00:22:55,412 --> 00:22:58,215
but I'd prefer it if you refrained
from doing that as much as possible.

284
00:23:00,484 --> 00:23:03,487
I'm doing this out of concern for you
and the company--

285
00:23:03,553 --> 00:23:05,355
I'm going to make this completely clear.

286
00:23:05,922 --> 00:23:10,126
If Keito wants to join the company
himself, I'd be happy to have him.

287
00:23:10,193 --> 00:23:11,228
However,

288
00:23:12,128 --> 00:23:14,364
the one who will succeed me is Mariko.

289
00:23:19,736 --> 00:23:21,905
You haven't forgotten, have you?

290
00:23:23,773 --> 00:23:27,944
That you and I share the same secret.

291
00:23:52,402 --> 00:23:54,638
IZUMI TAKEDA

292
00:23:55,906 --> 00:23:56,773
Hello?

293
00:23:57,507 --> 00:23:59,743
Did you find out anything regarding Asai?

294
00:23:59,809 --> 00:24:04,014
I was finally able to get through
to Asai's mother a moment ago,

295
00:24:04,748 --> 00:24:05,682
but…

296
00:24:07,517 --> 00:24:08,351
What?

297
00:24:44,287 --> 00:24:45,388
The food is here.

298
00:24:51,027 --> 00:24:52,362
Did you die?

299
00:24:56,499 --> 00:24:57,500
Eat.

300
00:25:28,031 --> 00:25:28,999
Good morning.

301
00:25:30,634 --> 00:25:31,534
Good morning.

302
00:25:40,543 --> 00:25:42,545
Were you waiting for me?

303
00:25:56,259 --> 00:25:58,061
<i>Doors are closing.</i>

304
00:26:08,571 --> 00:26:12,342
I don't think
there's any urgent work today.

305
00:26:18,948 --> 00:26:20,950
Is he waiting for me?

306
00:26:32,762 --> 00:26:33,663
Oh, are you finished?

307
00:26:35,799 --> 00:26:37,400
I just finished too.

308
00:26:38,001 --> 00:26:39,903
Would you like to walk
to the station together?

309
00:26:42,605 --> 00:26:45,075
Sure, why not?

310
00:26:53,083 --> 00:26:55,685
You're going home to watch
<i>Captain Marvel</i> right now?

311
00:26:57,887 --> 00:26:59,622
-Is there something wrong with that?
-No.

312
00:26:59,689 --> 00:27:00,690
It sounds fun.

313
00:27:01,491 --> 00:27:02,726
Mariko.

314
00:27:04,194 --> 00:27:05,061
Sayuri…

315
00:27:05,729 --> 00:27:07,163
Thanks for coming the other day.

316
00:27:07,697 --> 00:27:08,631
What's going on?

317
00:27:09,566 --> 00:27:11,735
I wanted to talk to you, Mariko.

318
00:27:12,235 --> 00:27:15,205
It's nothing major,
but I wanted to consult you about Keito.

319
00:27:15,271 --> 00:27:17,173
Do you have a moment right now?

320
00:27:17,774 --> 00:27:18,641
Yes.

321
00:27:20,076 --> 00:27:20,944
Let's go, then.

322
00:27:21,678 --> 00:27:23,246
-See you.
-Oh, yes.

323
00:27:39,129 --> 00:27:40,130
Excuse me.

324
00:27:45,969 --> 00:27:48,438
You're wearing that?

325
00:27:50,140 --> 00:27:51,274
Yes.

326
00:27:55,478 --> 00:27:56,412
I'm sorry.

327
00:27:57,547 --> 00:27:59,015
Your father told me about it.

328
00:27:59,716 --> 00:28:01,518
I thought I was doing something nice.

329
00:28:03,119 --> 00:28:03,987
No.

330
00:28:05,021 --> 00:28:08,691
I also reflected
on how childish I sounded.

331
00:28:09,759 --> 00:28:13,029
I'm actually happy
to be able to wear it like this.

332
00:28:16,866 --> 00:28:18,601
I'm sorry, Mariko.

333
00:28:21,104 --> 00:28:23,039
After your mother passed away,

334
00:28:23,106 --> 00:28:26,342
I thought I wanted to, and had to,

335
00:28:27,210 --> 00:28:29,312
become a mother to you.

336
00:28:30,079 --> 00:28:33,616
But that mindset itself
was hurting you, wasn't it?

337
00:28:37,086 --> 00:28:38,254
I'm sorry.

338
00:28:43,026 --> 00:28:44,127
Sayuri…

339
00:28:45,495 --> 00:28:46,429
Even so,

340
00:28:46,996 --> 00:28:50,300
I'm truly grateful
for how much you dote on Keito.

341
00:28:52,035 --> 00:28:53,469
Of course I do.

342
00:28:53,536 --> 00:28:55,104
Keito is my younger brother.

343
00:28:56,706 --> 00:28:59,676
When he joins the company next year,
please look after him.

344
00:29:01,778 --> 00:29:02,612
Yes.

345
00:29:11,221 --> 00:29:12,889
I'm sorry. It's a work call.

346
00:29:12,956 --> 00:29:14,924
-Go ahead, go ahead.
-Excuse me.

347
00:29:16,759 --> 00:29:19,796
Yes, hello? Yes, thank you as always.

348
00:30:26,896 --> 00:30:27,830
Mariko…

349
00:30:30,867 --> 00:30:31,701
Are you okay?

350
00:30:35,004 --> 00:30:36,039
Were you waiting?

351
00:30:38,841 --> 00:30:40,710
Sorry, I was worried.

352
00:30:43,947 --> 00:30:44,914
I'll walk you home.

353
00:30:45,481 --> 00:30:47,050
What? It's fine. I'll be okay.

354
00:30:47,116 --> 00:30:49,519
No, it's not that far anyway.

355
00:31:02,966 --> 00:31:06,970
Ah, yes. Yes.

356
00:31:09,072 --> 00:31:09,939
I thought so.

357
00:31:11,441 --> 00:31:12,542
He was there.

358
00:31:13,343 --> 00:31:15,778
Ah, no problem at all.
Thank you very much.

359
00:31:38,101 --> 00:31:39,402
Everyone,

360
00:31:39,469 --> 00:31:42,505
please pause your work
and step away from your computers.

361
00:31:43,339 --> 00:31:44,407
What is it?

362
00:31:46,409 --> 00:31:47,577
Don't touch your computers.

363
00:31:47,643 --> 00:31:49,879
Leave the power as it is.

364
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:52,248
What is going on?

365
00:31:52,849 --> 00:31:53,950
Manager Nose.

366
00:31:54,517 --> 00:31:56,319
An allegation has been made

367
00:31:56,386 --> 00:31:59,188
that you have been taking confidential
company information out of the office.

368
00:31:59,889 --> 00:32:02,492
Due to the urgent nature of this matter,
we need to temporarily halt operations.

369
00:32:02,558 --> 00:32:05,895
May we inspect
your company PC and smartphone?

370
00:32:07,430 --> 00:32:08,831
That's absurd!

371
00:32:08,898 --> 00:32:10,400
What kind of allegation--

372
00:32:10,466 --> 00:32:12,735
Go ahead. Please inspect them.

373
00:32:13,236 --> 00:32:14,570
Thank you.

374
00:32:25,982 --> 00:32:27,683
May we inspect your bag?

375
00:32:29,519 --> 00:32:30,620
I don't mind. Go ahead.

376
00:32:31,621 --> 00:32:32,889
Thank you.

377
00:32:34,791 --> 00:32:35,825
Thank you.

378
00:32:56,412 --> 00:32:58,347
I will open this.

379
00:33:15,264 --> 00:33:16,632
What was that about?

380
00:33:16,699 --> 00:33:19,001
That interrupted all our work.

381
00:33:19,068 --> 00:33:20,970
That was beyond rude.

382
00:33:21,037 --> 00:33:22,839
You should report this to management.

383
00:33:22,905 --> 00:33:24,574
But the investigation came
from the company itself.

384
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:26,375
Who would we even complain to?

385
00:33:28,277 --> 00:33:30,446
I'm sorry to say this,

386
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:32,248
but…

387
00:33:32,315 --> 00:33:35,985
someone who holds a grudge against Mariko
probably did this on purpose, right?

388
00:33:42,792 --> 00:33:44,527
-Where's Yukimura?
-Huh?

389
00:33:46,896 --> 00:33:48,998
Yukimura always seems to vanish
at moments like this.

390
00:33:55,271 --> 00:33:56,472
What do you mean?

391
00:33:57,640 --> 00:34:01,244
It should definitely be
in the pencil case inside her bag.

392
00:34:01,844 --> 00:34:02,912
Try again--

393
00:34:51,327 --> 00:34:54,363
You were the one who made that report
to the audit department, weren't you?

394
00:34:56,265 --> 00:34:57,099
What are you talking about?

395
00:35:04,073 --> 00:35:05,308
Look.

396
00:35:09,745 --> 00:35:13,649
I knew something was up
the moment you came to meet Mariko.

397
00:35:14,283 --> 00:35:15,418
Excuse me.

398
00:35:17,987 --> 00:35:19,388
Yes, hello.

399
00:35:36,839 --> 00:35:38,007
I'll walk you home.

400
00:35:38,074 --> 00:35:39,442
What? It's fine. I'll be okay.

401
00:35:39,508 --> 00:35:41,978
No, it's not that far anyway.

402
00:35:45,915 --> 00:35:47,984
When is the next bus coming?

403
00:35:51,854 --> 00:35:52,955
Let's see…

404
00:35:53,656 --> 00:35:58,060
BUS SCHEDULE

405
00:36:14,210 --> 00:36:19,849
This was packed with data
that would be catastrophic if leaked,

406
00:36:19,915 --> 00:36:24,020
like company customer lists, ingredient
formulas for our main product lines.

407
00:36:26,522 --> 00:36:28,524
Was this on Tateiwa's computer?

408
00:36:33,329 --> 00:36:35,898
That man was up
to far worse things than I imagined.

409
00:36:38,267 --> 00:36:42,605
Your plan was to pin all of this on Mariko
to drive her out of the company,

410
00:36:42,672 --> 00:36:43,639
wasn't it?

411
00:36:50,913 --> 00:36:52,548
She's in the way.

412
00:36:54,150 --> 00:36:55,618
She's just like her mother.

413
00:36:56,385 --> 00:36:59,522
Her mother just happened to be
lucky enough to marry a rich man.

414
00:37:00,156 --> 00:37:02,825
Yet she looked at me
with those pitying eyes.

415
00:37:04,660 --> 00:37:06,329
That girl has the exact same eyes.

416
00:37:07,196 --> 00:37:12,001
People born privileged look down on others
without even realizing it!

417
00:37:16,372 --> 00:37:17,907
But in the end…

418
00:37:19,709 --> 00:37:22,411
it just means you can't accomplish
anything on your own, right?

419
00:37:24,714 --> 00:37:25,781
You always

420
00:37:26,482 --> 00:37:30,119
try to use someone else's power
to get what you want.

421
00:37:31,554 --> 00:37:32,855
But Mariko is different.

422
00:37:34,357 --> 00:37:37,360
You and Mariko were never
on the same playing field to begin with.

423
00:37:42,732 --> 00:37:43,632
Um…

424
00:37:44,767 --> 00:37:50,306
I told you I wouldn't forgive anyone
who schemes against Mariko, didn't I?

425
00:38:10,359 --> 00:38:12,395
-Well, see you.
-Goodnight.

426
00:38:12,962 --> 00:38:13,929
Have a good night.

427
00:38:55,538 --> 00:38:56,705
MARIKO

428
00:38:56,772 --> 00:39:01,811
CAFFEINE THAT CALMS THE HEART

429
00:39:27,470 --> 00:39:29,505
MARIKO UPLOADED A NEW POST

430
00:39:35,845 --> 00:39:37,813
‎MARIKO

431
00:39:47,156 --> 00:39:48,457
‎They're the same…

432
00:40:01,437 --> 00:40:02,271
‎FIRST TIME COMING HERE

433
00:40:32,334 --> 00:40:34,169
You're Sayuri Nose, correct?

434
00:40:36,472 --> 00:40:38,107
You were the one who took

435
00:40:38,741 --> 00:40:41,210
Tateiwa's computer data
after the incident.

436
00:40:44,580 --> 00:40:46,348
To think President Nose's wife

437
00:40:47,116 --> 00:40:49,084
was the mistress.

438
00:40:50,352 --> 00:40:52,955
It took a lot of effort
to uncover your identity.

439
00:40:54,657 --> 00:40:57,092
I was trying to see you too.

440
00:40:59,595 --> 00:41:02,197
It took me a lot of effort
to uncover your identity as well.

441
00:41:05,534 --> 00:41:06,535
It was you, wasn't it?

442
00:41:07,503 --> 00:41:08,804
The one who killed Tateiwa.

443
00:41:12,041 --> 00:41:13,309
Why do you say that?

444
00:41:15,711 --> 00:41:17,513
I was the one who told Tateiwa

445
00:41:19,048 --> 00:41:20,215
to look into you.

446
00:41:20,282 --> 00:41:21,116
GORO KIKUTA OFFICE

447
00:41:21,817 --> 00:41:24,920
A suspicious man
is getting close to Mariko,

448
00:41:25,988 --> 00:41:28,324
but he looks somewhat familiar.

449
00:41:29,525 --> 00:41:31,427
Could you look into him?

450
00:41:32,494 --> 00:41:34,797
You have a wonderful…

451
00:41:36,298 --> 00:41:37,600
spotless record yourself.

452
00:41:37,666 --> 00:41:39,068
And you're from
a family of police officers.

453
00:41:40,002 --> 00:41:41,670
But I wonder how everyone would feel

454
00:41:42,338 --> 00:41:43,606
if they found out who you really are?

455
00:41:45,274 --> 00:41:47,276
I wonder what Mariko would think too.

456
00:41:48,177 --> 00:41:49,979
What are you talking about?

457
00:41:52,481 --> 00:41:53,849
The real me

458
00:41:54,650 --> 00:41:56,218
is exactly as written there,

459
00:41:57,219 --> 00:41:58,921
spotless, just as you said.

460
00:42:01,023 --> 00:42:03,258
In that case, why did you rush to meet me?

461
00:42:04,994 --> 00:42:08,597
Because the secret from 25 years ago

462
00:42:08,664 --> 00:42:12,001
that you've been protecting
is written right here, isn't it?

463
00:42:18,040 --> 00:42:20,209
That's why you killed Tateiwa.

464
00:42:24,546 --> 00:42:26,215
I remembered.

465
00:42:26,281 --> 00:42:28,250
Twenty-five years ago,

466
00:42:28,317 --> 00:42:30,119
you used to frequent the Nose household.

467
00:42:35,424 --> 00:42:36,392
Don't worry.

468
00:42:37,026 --> 00:42:40,362
I won't tell anyone about your crime.

469
00:42:41,096 --> 00:42:42,064
In exchange,

470
00:42:43,465 --> 00:42:44,800
kill that man.

471
00:42:45,534 --> 00:42:46,969
Sota Yukimura.

472
00:42:48,570 --> 00:42:50,272
Don't you find him to be an eyesore?

473
00:42:51,373 --> 00:42:54,910
If you kill him, the suspect dies,

474
00:42:54,977 --> 00:42:57,312
which benefits you too, right?

475
00:43:23,706 --> 00:43:25,808
Hello.

476
00:43:25,874 --> 00:43:29,044
There was an issue over
at general affairs, so I had to go.

477
00:43:42,891 --> 00:43:43,892
Mariko?

478
00:43:52,901 --> 00:43:55,637
Is this you?

479
00:44:01,944 --> 00:44:03,946
You've been following
my social media for years,

480
00:44:04,646 --> 00:44:06,682
years before we even met?

481
00:44:08,117 --> 00:44:10,886
What? What does this mean?

482
00:44:14,490 --> 00:44:15,390
That's…

483
00:44:59,468 --> 00:45:02,304
<i>Me disappearing is what's best for Mariko.</i>

484
00:45:02,371 --> 00:45:03,639
NEXT TIME…

